    "prose": "Rain hammered the covered route behind them, and wind drove the sound through the gallery entry. Aya kept both hands steady on her side of the mosaic panel. Across from her, Mert maintained the same careful hold.\n\n“The door is wide enough,” Aya said. “Same pace as before?”\n\nMert nodded. “Same pace.”\n\nTogether, without loosening their shared hold, Aya and Mert carried the restored fragile panel through the wide open gallery door from the gallery entry into the display alcove. Their steps stayed slow and matched. The panel remained level and intact between them for the whole crossing.\n\nThey stopped in front of the fixed display mount.\n\n“Ready to lower it?” Mert asked.\n\nAya checked his stance, then met his eyes. “Ready. Together.”\n\nAya and Mert lowered the mosaic panel onto the fixed mount. They guided it into place at the same time, keeping their hands on it until it rested securely. Only then did Aya release her side. Mert released his. The same restored panel stood intact on display.\n\nFor a moment, they both looked at the finished mosaic while the rain beat harder outside.\n\nAya flexed her tired fingers. “I wanted to do this alone at first,” she said. “That would have been a mistake.”\n\nMert turned toward her and listened.\n\n“You matched my pace, and you helped keep it steady all the way,” Aya continued. “We got it here safely because we carried it carefully together. Thank you.”\n\nMert gave a small, tired smile. “You kept it steady too.”\n\nAya nodded. They were still classmates, not suddenly best friends, but the trust between them no longer felt like a guess.",
